{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CetHqvTUdaoNHe7aqfVHD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect. Now I have all the information I need. Let me summarize my analysis:\n\n**Repository findings:**\n- Shipment model (Shipment.kt:9-14): has shipmentId, orderId, carrier, status\n- ShipmentStatus enum (Shipment.kt:23-27): CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED\n- ShipmentController (ShipmentController.kt): currently has create, getById, list endpoints\n- InMemoryShipmentRepository (ShipmentRepository.kt:11-27): save, existsById, findById, findAll, clear\n- Error handling (ApiExceptions.kt:23, 19): ConflictException (409), ResourceNotFoundException (404)\n- ErrorCode enum (ApiError.kt:31-37): ORDER_NOT_FOUND, ORDER_ALREADY_EXISTS, SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS, VALIDATION_FAILED\n- GlobalExceptionHandler (GlobalExceptionHandler.kt): converts ApiException to ApiError response\n\n**Conventions this repository has:**\n- Controllers throw ApiExceptions; GlobalExceptionHandler catches and converts them\n- ConflictException(ErrorCode.*, message) for 409 responses\n- ResourceNotFoundException(ErrorCode.*, message) for 404 responses\n- ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.CREATED).body(saved) for creation returns\n- Plain response body (no ResponseEntity wrapper) for successful fetches\n- Tests use MockMvc with jsonPath assertions, check error.code for failures\n- Tests clear repository in @BeforeEach, use helper methods for building requests\n- Tests must verify state through a separate GET after mutation (testing-and-verification skill requirements)\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. **ShipmentController.kt** - Must add POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm endpoint. Cannot be avoided: this is where the endpoint lives.\n2. **ApiError.kt** - Must add ErrorCode enum value for invalid state transitions (409 case). Cannot be avoided: need a distinct code for \"cannot confirm cancelled shipment\".\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** - Must add tests covering all four cases. Cannot be avoided: acceptance criteria requires test coverage.\n\n**Risks:**\n1. Response body might not match persisted state if testing is incomplete (testing-and-verification skill mitigates this)\n2. Idempotency could fail if CONFIRMED→CONFIRMED transition isn't tested properly\n3. The confirm endpoint might not persist changes correctly if not verified through separate GET request\n\n**Open questions:**\n- What ErrorCode name should I use for the \"cannot confirm cancelled shipment\" case? The ticket says responses should be \"consistent with the rest of this API\" but doesn't name a specific code. Given the existing pattern (SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS), I'll add SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE as the new code. This seems reasonable as a state constraint violation distinct from existence issues.\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n\n**Proposed change by file:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt**: Add `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE` to the ErrorCode enum. This will be thrown when attempting to confirm a shipment in CANCELLED status (409 Conflict).\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt**: Add a new endpoint method `confirm(@PathVariable shipmentId: String): ResponseEntity<Shipment>` that:\n   - Finds the shipment by ID → throws ResourceNotFoundException(SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND) if not found\n   - If status is CANCELLED → throws ConflictException(SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE)\n   - If status is CREATED → updates it to CONFIRMED and saves\n   - If status is CONFIRMED → returns it unchanged (idempotent)\n   - Returns ResponseEntity.ok(updated) with the final shipment\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt**: Add four new test methods covering:\n   - `confirms a CREATED shipment to CONFIRMED` → asserts response body contains status CONFIRMED, then GETs the shipment to verify persistence\n   - `idempotently confirms an already CONFIRMED shipment` → confirms once, then confirms again and asserts both responses are identical, then GETs to verify state is unchanged\n   - `rejects confirming a CANCELLED shipment with error code` → attempts confirm, asserts 409 status and error.code=SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE, then GETs to verify shipment state is unchanged\n   - `reports unknown shipment` → attempts confirm on non-existent ID, asserts 404 status and error.code=SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\n\n**Alternative rejected:**\n- I considered putting the state transition logic in a service layer, but the codebase has no service classes—controllers directly use repositories. This matches the existing OrderController and CustomerController patterns. Adding a service would be unrelated refactoring outside the scope.\n- I considered reusing an existing ErrorCode (like VALIDATION_FAILED) for the CANCELLED case, but it should be HTTP 409 (Conflict), not 400 (Bad Request). The existing 409 codes (SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS) all use ConflictException. A new ErrorCode is cleaner and follows the existing pattern.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n- **Success case (CREATED→CONFIRMED)**: Controller receives POST /shipments/{id}/confirm → queries repository.findById(id) → not null → checks status == CREATED → updates status to CONFIRMED → repository.save(updated) → returns ResponseEntity.ok(updated shipment)\n\n- **Idempotent case (CONFIRMED→CONFIRMED)**: Same as above, but status == CONFIRMED → returns the existing shipment unchanged → ResponseEntity.ok(existing shipment)\n\n- **Cancelled case**: Controller receives POST /shipments/{id}/confirm → queries repository.findById(id) → not null → checks status == CANCELLED → throws ConflictException(SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE, message) → GlobalExceptionHandler catches it → returns 409 with error.code=SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE. State remains CANCELLED.\n\n- **Not found case**: Controller receives POST /shipments/{id}/confirm → queries repository.findById(id) → returns null → throws ResourceNotFoundException(SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, message) → GlobalExceptionHandler catches it → returns 404 with error.code=SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n1. **Confirm CREATED shipment**: Create shipment in CREATED status → POST confirm → assert response body status=CONFIRMED → GET the shipment → assert it's now CONFIRMED\n2. **Idempotent confirm**: Create shipment → confirm once → confirm twice → assert both responses have status CONFIRMED → GET → assert still CONFIRMED\n3. **Reject CANCELLED**: Manually create CANCELLED shipment via repository → POST confirm → assert 409 status → assert error.code=SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE → GET → assert still CANCELLED\n4. **Reject unknown**: POST confirm on non-existent ID → assert 404 status → assert error.code=SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n\nNow I'll implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":507,"cache_read_input_tokens":22726,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":507},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b6994d43-2180-4380-ae20-e262e9ff9139","uuid":"378c196b-a47d-498a-986d-356fea13be42","timestamp":"2026-09-09T17:52:34.380Z","request_id":"req_011CetHquqGk6KjE5osAD5Nh"}
